# Data Model

## Sources of Truth
List authoritative stores and which entities/fields each owns.

## Core Entities
For each entity document:
- stable identifier,
- owner/tenant relationship,
- lifecycle,
- required invariants,
- important relationships.

## Persistence Boundaries
Document repositories/adapters, external stores, caches, queues, files, spreadsheets, or APIs that persist/derive data.

## Data Integrity Rules
List uniqueness, referential, calculation, ordering, idempotency, and non-overwrite requirements.

## Migrations
Document compatibility, backup, rollback, validation, and dual-read/write requirements where applicable.

## Retention / Deletion
Record retention, deletion, archival, and recovery rules.

## Exports / Imports
Document format/contracts and any security/tenant scoping requirements.

## Known Gaps / Unknowns
Unverified legacy behavior stays explicit until inspected.
